{"content":[{"c":["GAD (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of the 12 sons of Jacob (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.26","r":"Gen.35.26","rawR":"Gen.35.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.26","value":"Gen.35.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 35:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.2","r":"1Chr.2.2","rawR":"1Chr.2.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.2","value":"1Chr.2.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:2"},"). He was the first of the two sons born to Jacob by Zilpah, Leah’s maid. Delighted with giving Jacob another son, Leah named the boy Gad, meaning “good fortune” (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.30.11","r":"Gen.30.11","rawR":"Gen.30.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.30.11","value":"Gen.30.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 30:11"},"). Later, Gad moved his family with Jacob to Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.1.4","r":"Exod.1.4","rawR":"Exod.1.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.1.4","value":"Exod.1.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 1:4"},"). When Jacob blessed his sons, he predicted that Gad would constantly be troubled by foreign invaders but would successfully withstand them and put them to flight (see ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.49.19","r":"Gen.49.19","rawR":"Gen.49.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.49.19","value":"Gen.49.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 49:19"}," and discussion below under Gad, Tribe of). Gad became the father of seven sons (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.16","r":"Gen.46.16","rawR":"Gen.46.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.16","value":"Gen.46.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:16"},") and the founder of the Gadites (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.12,16","r":"Deut.3.12,16","rawR":"Deut.3.12,16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.12,16","value":"Deut.3.12,16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:12, 16"},"), one of the 12 tribes of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Num.2.14","r":"Num.2.14","rawR":"Num.2.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.14","value":"Num.2.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 2:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GadTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GadTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GadTribeof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Gad, Tribe of"},"."],"sourceClass":"sp","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Prophet and seer during the reign of David. He counseled David to leave Mizpeh of Moab and return to the land of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.5","r":"1Sam.22.5","rawR":"1Sam.22.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.5","value":"1Sam.22.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 22:5"},"). Gad communicated David’s punishment for numbering the fighting men of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.24.11-14,18-19","r":"2Sam.24.11-14,18-19","rawR":"2Sam.24.11-14,18-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.24.11-14,18-19","value":"2Sam.24.11-14,18-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 24:11-14, 18-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.21.9-19","r":"1Chr.21.9-19","rawR":"1Chr.21.9-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.21.9-19","value":"1Chr.21.9-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 21:9-19"},"), assisted David and Nathan in setting up the order of worship in the sanctuary (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.25","r":"2Chr.29.25","rawR":"2Chr.29.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.25","value":"2Chr.29.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:25"},") and later wrote an account of David’s life (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.29.29","r":"1Chr.29.29","rawR":"1Chr.29.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.29.29","value":"1Chr.29.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 29:29"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"GadPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 35:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.35.26","rawQueryValue":"Gen.35.26","sourceRefExact":"Gen.35.26"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.2","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.2","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.2"},{"anchorText":"Gn 30:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.30.11","rawQueryValue":"Gen.30.11","sourceRefExact":"Gen.30.11"},{"anchorText":"Ex 1:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.1.4","rawQueryValue":"Exod.1.4","sourceRefExact":"Exod.1.4"},{"anchorText":"Gn 49:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.49.19","rawQueryValue":"Gen.49.19","sourceRefExact":"Gen.49.19"},{"anchorText":"Gn 46:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.16","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.16","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.16"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:12, 16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.12,16","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.12,16","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.12,16"},{"anchorText":"Nm 2:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.2.14","rawQueryValue":"Num.2.14","sourceRefExact":"Num.2.14"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 22:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.5","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.5","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.5"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 24:11-14, 18-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.24.11-14,18-19","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.24.11-14,18-19","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.24.11-14,18-19"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 21:9-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.21.9-19","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.21.9-19","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.21.9-19"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 29:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.29.25","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.29.25","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.29.25"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 29:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.29.29","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.29.29","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.29.29"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"513912068a10d646802f28f16a0c14c5f67057ed150fb